WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:03.360
High Sparrow: Are you prepared to stand trial

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:05.420
and profess your guilt

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:07.620
or innocence before the Seven?

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:13.940
Jon Snow: We need to trust each other.

00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:16.020
We have so many enemies now.

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:20.080
Walder Frey: The Freys and the Lannisters,

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:21.620
send their regards.

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:23.420
Sansa Stark: What do you want?

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:24.660
Littlefinger: I thought you knew what I wanted.

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:26.800
Davos Seaworth: Tell him what you did to him.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:28.040
Tell him!

00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:29.860
Are you afraid?

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:30.720
Good.

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:32.980
Tyrion Lannister: You're in the great game now.

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:35.980
And the great game's terrifying.

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:41.320
Hey YouTubers, it's Charlie.

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:42.580
This is gonna be my Game of Thrones

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:43.660
finale trailer video.

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:44.520
Just careful for spoilers,

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:47.040
for everything that's happened on the show so far.

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:48.000
So, here we go.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.000
The funny thing that happened this season is that HBO,

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:51.840
at a certain point, for the last couple of episodes,

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:54.500
stopped releasing information, synopsis

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:56.180
but eventually we learned the synopsis

00:00:56.180 --> 00:00:57.360
for the finale is just

00:00:57.420 --> 00:00:59.340
"Cersei faces her trial."

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:00.420
Very simple.

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:02.060
Obviously there's a whole lot more going on,

00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:03.520
and we see that from the trailer.

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:04.780
They're using the finale to

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:06.820
wrap up all the big ongoing storylines

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:08.520
from this season, and tee up

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:09.960
what's going to be happening next season.

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:12.580
So, just kind of moving the chess pieces around the board on Westeros.

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:14.480
Because that's where most people are going to be.

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:17.720
The end of Episode 9 is Daenerys is leaving Mereen

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:21.160
makes it sound like she's not planning on coming back anytime soon

00:01:21.160 --> 00:01:24.180
"Tell everyone what Daenerys did when she came to Meereen,

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:26.800
and don't try to go back to your slaver's ways."

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:28.820
So, it was like Tyrion was giving the Great Master

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:30.520
that they left alive a warning.

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:32.760
If you don't uphold the terms of your surrender,

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:35.720
no more slavery will come back with the dragons.

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:38.100
So it seems like the action for the final two seasons -

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:39.580
I mean, as far that we know there's gonna be

00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:40.960
a Season 7 and a Season 8 -

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:42.940
will take place in Westeros and obviously

00:01:42.940 --> 00:01:44.440
moving closer and closer to the North

00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:46.560
wherever the Night King's army happens to be.

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:48.720
And the really interesting thing about this trailer too

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:51.360
is this 'reverse Red Wedding' that they're teasing

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:52.260
with Jaime's character

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:53.940
just like he could not give a shit

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:55.120
about Walder Frey.

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:57.340
"The Lannisters and the Freys send their regards."

00:01:57.340 --> 00:02:00.020
Just this really horrific twist on the Red Wedding.

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:02.580
So, if you've ever hoped for a Jaime redemption,

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:04.120
this is the moment to hope for.

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:05.660
A 'reverse Red Wedding'.

00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:08.060
"Catelyn Stark sends her regards."

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:09.060
But on the flipside of that,

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:10.120
Cersei's character.

00:02:10.120 --> 00:02:13.600
There was so much teasing of Cersei's storyline in Episode 9.

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:14.480
It was so funny.

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:16.360
So, in the first five minutes of the episode,

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:20.040
Tyrion specifically mentions the wildfire that's hidden

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:21.360
all over King's Landing.

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:23.880
The story that Jaime told him about the Mad King.

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:25.080
So he's like, Daenerys,

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:27.700
don't burn these cities, don't be like your father.

00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:29.280
We don't want to go that far.

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:31.720
I want to suggest an alternative approach.

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:33.360
But it seems like Cersei

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:35.840
isn't going to listen to that kind of reason.

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:39.100
So she is going to do what Daenerys had planned to do.

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:41.160
"Whoa, you're going full Mad Queen."

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:43.440
So it seems like Cersei is going to have her 'Mad Queen' moment

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:46.140
because there is a big hidden cache of wildfire

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:48.080
underneath the Great Sept

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:51.020
and that's where most of the action for her storyline's gonna take place.

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:52.540
But as I've mentioned before,

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:55.480
Cersei is the protagonist of her own storyline

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:58.600
and we're viewing all this King's Landing stuff through her eyes.

00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:00.940
So, don't you feel like the wildfire is her out,

00:03:00.940 --> 00:03:02.440
she'll come away with a big victory

00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:04.440
but there'll be so much collateral damage

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:06.380
and so many good people will die

00:03:06.380 --> 00:03:08.080
that she'll seem like a villain.

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:10.140
So the show's really ambiguous at times about

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:11.200
what's good, what's evil,

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:13.220
it's really all about people's motivation,

00:03:13.220 --> 00:03:16.080
the things that they fight for, how compelling their characters are.

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:19.120
So while there is a couple of really big villains on the show right now,

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:21.080
there is the Night King, there is Euron Greyjoy -

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:22.940
who's going to be a pretty fantastic villain -

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:24.240
and then there is Cersei Lannister.

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:26.620
I will argue that Cersei Lannister is gonna be

00:03:26.620 --> 00:03:29.500
the best human villain on the show after this season.

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:31.880
And like I've said, the finale is kinda intended to

00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:33.960
create some context for where the next season is

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:34.760
gonna pick up.

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:36.180
I think if anyone who has gonna have the job of

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:38.040
taking Cersei down, it should be Jaime

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:40.900
so you could tie that into Maggie the Frog Prophecy

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:42.040
'Valonqar'.

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:43.180
But I think, the idea with that -

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:44.960
like, if you're just going by the TV show's version,

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:47.400
which is a slightly simpler version that the book did,

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:49.320
they really didn't do the 'Valonqar' on the TV show -

00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:51.560
but Maggie the Frog was telling Cersei

00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:53.800
that all these terrible things were gonna happen to her.

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:55.700
But I think what the finale is going to show us

00:03:55.700 --> 00:03:59.020
is that she's gonna to have brung about all those terrible things.

00:03:59.020 --> 00:04:01.740
Like, ultimately she'll be the cause of her own downfall,

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:03.160
the death of all her children.

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:05.560
So the Maggie the Frog Prophecy is kind of like a

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:08.560
'self-fulfilling' prophecy, at least in the context of the TV show.

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:10.000
It's a little more complex in the books.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:11.560
But what about Sansa and Littlefinger?

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:14.200
I know a lot of people were confused about her actions

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:16.600
going into the Battle of Winterfell, like why didn't she

00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:19.300
tell Jon about the alliance that she formed with Littlefinger,

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:22.020
and what is the price that he is going to extract from this?

00:04:22.020 --> 00:04:24.000
Like, she just didn't get all that soldiers for free.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:26.600
So logically, I think what Littlefinger's plan is

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:28.980
is to marry her to Sweetrobin

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:30.700
so that he could control both of them.

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:33.300
Sansa isn't quite as controllable as Sweetrobin.

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:36.100
Sweetrobin's kind of like a human potato, just like Tommen,

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:38.300
you can pick them up and put them wherever you want them -

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:39.580
they'll do what you want them to do.

00:04:39.580 --> 00:04:42.260
So Littlefinger firmly has the forces of the Vale

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:43.160
under his thumb.

00:04:43.160 --> 00:04:45.480
And I think, now with this alliance with Sansa,

00:04:45.480 --> 00:04:47.980
he'll have the forces of the North under his thumb too,

00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:50.040
but not necessarily in a sinister way.

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:51.700
I think, if he had his way,

00:04:51.700 --> 00:04:54.800
he would put Sansa on the Iron Throne with Sweetrobin,

00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:56.680
he would become the new Hand of the King

00:04:56.680 --> 00:04:58.980
and by proxy, control the Seven Kingdoms.

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:01.240
But the problem is, is if Cersei blows up

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:02.900
half of King's Landing with wildfire,

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:04.780
there really isn't going to be an Iron Throne

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:06.840
and I think Daenerys is probably gonna realise that

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:09.460
that isn't the ultimate goal when she gets to Westeros too.

00:05:09.460 --> 00:05:12.280
So I think the Iron Throne will become less of a priority

00:05:12.280 --> 00:05:14.780
and it'll be more about uniting the Seven Kingdoms

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:17.240
against this bigger threat of the Night King.

00:05:17.240 --> 00:05:19.720
What about Jon Snow, Tower of Joy reveal?

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:21.780
Like, why would the show wait that long -

00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:23.880
I mean, it's a great fan moment, it's a bit of fan service

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:25.500
because we've been expecting it for so long -

00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:28.040
but why would the show save this for the very end?

00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:29.780
Well, if you think about what Cersei's doing,

00:05:29.780 --> 00:05:33.060
if Tommen's collateral damage and there is no King,

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:35.420
then there's no leadership and right now,

00:05:35.420 --> 00:05:37.520
Jon Snow - now that he has defeated Ramsay -

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:39.960
he's probably isn't too sure what he's gonna do.

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:42.180
It's not like he's gonna take the black again,

00:05:42.180 --> 00:05:44.500
so I think the reveal is meant to tee up

00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:48.320
Jon Snow having a higher purpose in the grand scheme of things.

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:50.420
He's like,  "What am I supposed to do with my life now?

00:05:50.420 --> 00:05:52.220
I'm part of some giant prophecy."

00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:54.500
So I think the TV show might give him some of

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:57.140
the Aegon storyline from the books that they cut out.

00:05:57.140 --> 00:05:58.980
Just someone as Varys says,

00:05:58.980 --> 00:06:02.120
with the right name, and someone that the people love.

00:06:02.120 --> 00:06:04.020
So think about what Jon Snow has done.

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:06.660
Even Ramsay was like, "I've heard stories about you and

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:07.840
the great things that you've done."

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:10.500
So that's probably going to spread across the Seven Kingdoms.

00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:12.500
People will hear about the awesome things that

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:13.360
Jon Snow has done.

00:06:13.360 --> 00:06:16.560
So maybe - fan fiction here - Varys will try to rope him

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:18.380
into the Targaryen Restoration.

00:06:18.380 --> 00:06:19.880
But what about Bran's storyline?

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:21.900
He's gonna be facing the Night King at The Wall.

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:24.660
I think we're gonna see him activate some of his new powers

00:06:24.660 --> 00:06:26.140
that he hasn't played around with

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:27.580
as the new last Greenseer,

00:06:27.580 --> 00:06:29.900
so I think we're gonna see Bran do some really cool stuff.

00:06:29.900 --> 00:06:32.220
And they'll do a pretty good job of foreshadowing

00:06:32.220 --> 00:06:34.600
what's gonna be happening with the Night's King next season.

00:06:34.600 --> 00:06:36.360
Tyrion talking about the wildfire -

00:06:36.360 --> 00:06:38.780
like, specifically mentioning wildfire

00:06:38.780 --> 00:06:40.720
underneath Baelor's Sept in Episode 9 -

00:06:40.720 --> 00:06:43.280
is a good example of how the show just like, slaps you

00:06:43.320 --> 00:06:46.220
in the face with stuff it's gonna be doing in the future

00:06:46.220 --> 00:06:48.500
So I think they're gonna do a good job of that in Episode 10.

00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:50.160
You'll have a really good idea for

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:51.260
what's gonna be happening in the first

00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:52.780
couple of episodes in the next season.

00:06:52.780 --> 00:06:54.520
So I'll just - I'll actually say there's a new round

00:06:54.520 --> 00:06:55.420
of the giveaway this week,

00:06:55.420 --> 00:06:57.780
all you have to do to enter is be a subscriber

00:06:57.780 --> 00:06:59.120
and leave a comment on this video.

00:06:59.120 --> 00:07:01.320
I'll announce the winner when I post my Q&amp;A video

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:02.300
in like, another day or two.

00:07:02.300 --> 00:07:04.320
But I also wanted to say, what's gonna be different

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:07.740
about this year? Obviously the finale is called 'Winds of Winter',

00:07:07.740 --> 00:07:09.320
but Winds of Winter - the book -

00:07:09.320 --> 00:07:10.820
is supposed to come out sometime.

00:07:10.820 --> 00:07:12.820
It might not come out 'til the end of the summer,

00:07:12.820 --> 00:07:15.800
but when it does, I will do videos about book things

00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:17.000
so we can compare some of the moments -

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:19.180
like the Hodor 'hold the door' moment.

00:07:19.180 --> 00:07:20.980
They said that the way that's gonna play out

00:07:20.980 --> 00:07:22.380
in the books is gonna be very different.

00:07:22.380 --> 00:07:24.660
So I'll do videos like that whenever that book comes out

00:07:24.660 --> 00:07:26.280
but that might not be for a couple of more months.

00:07:26.280 --> 00:07:29.100
So the bonus videos I do for the TV show will depend

00:07:29.100 --> 00:07:31.040
a lot on what you guys want to talk about,

00:07:31.040 --> 00:07:32.020
and then whenever the book drops,

00:07:32.020 --> 00:07:33.220
we can talk about book stuff.

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:34.820
It'll be alot of fun, there's a whole bunch of

00:07:34.820 --> 00:07:37.020
really cool book stuff, the show's never gonna have time

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:37.680
to touch.

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:39.940
But this weekend, this week we'll have alot of fun

00:07:39.940 --> 00:07:41.940
talking about how the show is metaphorically

00:07:41.940 --> 00:07:45.320
'burning down the practises of the old way' of doing things

00:07:45.320 --> 00:07:47.460
to make way for the new, and how it's literally

00:07:47.460 --> 00:07:50.260
burning things down. Like Daenerys, burning the Khals,

00:07:50.260 --> 00:07:53.940
and hopefully seeing wildfire burn down a lot of King's Landing.

00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:55.900
So while you guys wait for my next videos to post

00:07:55.900 --> 00:07:56.520
you can click here (Lyanna Mormont's game face)

00:07:56.520 --> 00:07:57.740
for last night's Episode 9 video

00:07:57.740 --> 00:07:59.080
and you can click here (Bran being Bran)

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:00.440
for a Tower of Joy refresher.

00:08:00.440 --> 00:08:01.560
Thank you so much for watching.

00:08:01.560 --> 00:08:02.760
Everybody, let's high five.

00:08:02.760 --> 00:08:03.940
I'll see you guys tonight.

